# logpush's settings for the brixOS image a person builds for their own
# machine: the name of their private repository and a token for it
# (projects/brix/README.md, "The kernel log handed over"). A secret:
# never in a commit. Nor what an editor leaves beside the file while and
# after it is written (logpush.local~, logpush.local.bak, a .txt a
# system's editor adds, vim's .logpush.local.swp, emacs's
# #logpush.local# and .#logpush.local), nor a copy the person keeps
# (logpush.local2, logpush.local-old): each holds the token too. The
# build takes the file from the top directory alone; a file of these
# names is ignored wherever it lies, a misplaced one as well.
logpush.local*
.logpush.local*
[#]logpush.local[#]
.[#]logpush.local

